Keep the engine alive while the text console waits for a line.

WHY (measured, not guessed). With --enable-text-console the debugger blocks in
`fgets(stdin)`, and while it is blocked ScummVM services nothing: no events, no time.
That is invisible until a guard row is driven, and then it stops dead in one place --

    before: warn=0x0000 g130=0x0000 has_pie=1
    after : warn=0x0000 g130=0x0001 has_pie=1   <- arm entered, printed, then parked

A backtrace taken at that moment names the culprit exactly:

    6: script 0   - ego::handleEvent      <- the guarded arm
    7: script 0   - call 62b              <- the message printer
    8: script 300 - export 0              <- PrintScript's proc300_0
    9: script 300 - call 8d
    a: script 300 - call 1f6

`proc300_0` is `(DoAudio 2 ...)` followed by a wait that only runs `(if (> temp0 0))` --
the CD speech. The engine only advances during `debug_countdown` bursts, and between
every burst the debugger sits in `fgets` with the clock stopped, so the speech never
finishes and the guard's refusal (emitted AFTER the print) is never reached. Muting
speech does not help; nor does un-muting it.

So: poll stdin instead of blocking on it, and between polls pump events and let time
pass. This is what `readline_eventFunction` already does for the readline build, except
that hook only runs while readline is waiting AT THE PROMPT.

FOR LOCAL DEBUGGING ONLY -- never shipped, never sent upstream from here.

APPLIES TO: gui/debugger.cpp, the plain-fgets branch of Debugger::enter().
APPLY WITH: (cd tools/scummvm-ref && git apply ../scummvm-patches/0001-*.patch)

MEASURED EFFECT. Before, a guard row parked forever at the print however many
`debug_countdown` bursts it got. After, execution continues past it -- the run reaches
IconBar::dispatchEvent, which it never did before.

⚠️ LIMIT: this covers the debugger WAITING FOR A LINE. It does NOT cover a print raised
inside `cmdSend`'s re-entrant run_vm, because the debugger is not at a prompt there --
so `send <obj> handleEvent <ev>` on a speaking handler still hangs. The click path is
the one this unblocks.

diff --git a/gui/debugger.cpp b/gui/debugger.cpp
index b37c84ad..075a7937 100644
--- a/gui/debugger.cpp
+++ b/gui/debugger.cpp
@@ -43,6 +43,12 @@
 	#include <readline/readline.h>
 	#include <readline/history.h>
 	#include "common/events.h"
+#else
+	// LOCAL DEBUGGING PATCH -- see tools/scummvm-patches/. Needed so the text console can wait
+	// for a line WITHOUT stopping the engine.
+	#include "common/events.h"
+	#include <unistd.h>
+	#include <sys/select.h>
 #endif
 
 
@@ -279,6 +285,27 @@ void Debugger::enter() {
 	do {
 		printf("debug> ");
 		::fflush(stdout);
+
+		// LOCAL DEBUGGING PATCH. Blocking in fgets() stops the engine dead: no events, no time.
+		// A game waiting on anything real-time -- CD speech, a timed dialog -- therefore never
+		// finishes, and any script parked behind it never resumes, however many
+		// `debug_countdown` bursts it is given. Poll stdin instead, and let the engine breathe
+		// between polls. (readline builds get this from rl_event_hook; this is the same idea for
+		// the plain-fgets path.)
+		for (;;) {
+			fd_set fds;
+			FD_ZERO(&fds);
+			FD_SET(STDIN_FILENO, &fds);
+			struct timeval tv = {0, 0};
+			if (select(STDIN_FILENO + 1, &fds, nullptr, nullptr, &tv) > 0)
+				break;                          // a line is waiting
+			Common::Event event;
+			while (g_system->getEventManager()->pollEvent(event)) {
+				// drop them: the game is paused at a prompt, but time must still pass
+			}
+			g_system->delayMillis(10);
+		}
+
 		if (!fgets(buf, sizeof(buf), stdin))
 			return;
 
